% One rule governs this file: an entry appears here only when the source was
% actually retrieved and read. docs/references.md is the ledger, it carries the
% retrieval date and the HTTP status observed from the build machine for every
% entry below, and a citation this project has not read appears in neither
% file. A plausible looking citation to a paper nobody opened is worse than no
% citation, because it survives review by looking exactly like a real one.
